IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `coa-core`

-- coa5-residential-addresses.l4: Companies Act 2006, Part 10, Chapter 8, "Directors' residential addresses: protection from disclosure": ss 240 to 246
-- (lines 3179-3263 of ukpga-2006-46.txt). The registrar is an official: his provisions (ss 242, 243, 245, 246) are encoded for what they decide, and the seat
-- layer asks them only for what they mean to the individual (what the registrar may do with a director's address, what notice the director is given).
--
-- SOURCE: a plain-text rendering of the Act from legislation.gov.uk made by a converter script; not the official text.
-- HOW TO READ AN ANSWER: see coa5-loans-exceptions.l4 (JUST TRUE, JUST FALSE and NOTHING as the rule of 2026-10-29 reads them).

§ `Chapter 8: directors' residential addresses (ss 240 to 246)`

-- ======================================================================================================================
-- s 240 Protected information
-- ======================================================================================================================

DECLARE `s 240(1) information` IS ONE OF
    `s 240(1)(a) information as to his usual residential address`
    `s 240(1)(b) the information that his service address is his usual residential address`
    `s 240(1) other information`

-- src:3181 | (1) This Chapter makes provision for protecting, in the case of a company director who is an individual—
-- src:3182 | (a) information as to his usual residential address;
-- src:3183 | (b) the information that his service address is his usual residential address.
-- src:3184 | (2) That information is referred to in this Chapter as “protected information”.
@ref s 240(1) and (2) protected information (src:3181-3184)
GIVEN information IS A `s 240(1) information`
      `it concerns a company director who is an individual` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 240(2) the information is protected information` MEANS
    IF `it concerns a company director who is an individual` AND (NOT (information EQUALS `s 240(1) other information`))
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "in the case of a company director who is an individual— (a) information as to his usual residential address; (b) the information that his service address is his usual residential address. That information is referred to in this Chapter as “protected information”"

-- src:3185 | (3) Information does not cease to be protected information on the individual ceasing to be a director of the company.
-- src:3186 | References in this Chapter to a director include, to that extent, a former director.
@ref s 240(3) protection continues (src:3185-3186)
GIVEN `the information was protected information while he was a director` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the individual has ceased to be a director of the company` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 240(3) the information ceases to be protected information` MEANS
    IF `the information was protected information while he was a director` AND `the individual has ceased to be a director of the company`
    THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Information does not cease to be protected information on the individual ceasing to be a director of the company"
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "on the individual ceasing to be a director of the company"

-- src:3186 | References in this Chapter to a director include, to that extent, a former director.
@ref s 240(3) a reference to a director includes a former director (src:3186-3186)
GIVEN `the person is a former director` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 240(3) a reference in this Chapter to a director includes the person` MEANS
    IF `the person is a former director`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (includes): "References in this Chapter to a director include, to that extent, a former director"

-- ======================================================================================================================
-- s 241 Protected information: restriction on use or disclosure by company
-- ======================================================================================================================

DECLARE `s 241(1) purpose of the use or disclosure` IS ONE OF
    `s 241(1)(a) communicating with the director concerned`
    `s 241(1)(b) complying with a requirement of the Companies Acts as to particulars to be sent to the registrar`
    `s 241(1)(c) disclosure in accordance with section 244 (disclosure under court order)`
    `s 241(1) another purpose`

-- src:3192 | (2) Subsection (1) does not prohibit any use or disclosure of protected information with the consent of the director concerned.
@ref s 241(2) consent (src:3192-3192)
GIVEN `the director concerned has consented to the use or disclosure` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 241(2) subsection (1) prohibits the use or disclosure` MEANS
    IF `the director concerned has consented to the use or disclosure`
    THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Subsection (1) does not prohibit any use or disclosure of protected information with the consent of the director concerned"
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "with the consent of the director concerned"

-- src:3188 | (1) A company must not use or disclose protected information about any of its directors, except—
-- src:3189 | (a) for communicating with the director concerned,
-- src:3190 | (b) in order to comply with any requirement of the Companies Acts as to particulars to be sent to the registrar, or
-- src:3191 | (c) in accordance with section 244 (disclosure under court order).
@ref s 241(1) the company may not use or disclose protected information (src:3188-3191)
GIVEN purpose IS A `s 241(1) purpose of the use or disclosure`
      `the information is protected information about one of the company's directors` IS A BOOLEAN
      `s 241(2) subsection (1) prohibits the use or disclosure` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 241(1) the company may not use or disclose the protected information` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `the information is protected information about one of the company's directors`
        THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "protected information about any of its directors"
        IF NOT (purpose EQUALS `s 241(1) another purpose`)
        THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "A company must not use or disclose protected information about any of its directors, except— (a) for communicating with the director concerned, (b) in order to comply with any requirement of the Companies Acts as to particulars to be sent to the registrar, or (c) in accordance with section 244"
        IF `s 241(2) subsection (1) prohibits the use or disclosure` EQUALS JUST FALSE
        THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Subsection (1) does not prohibit any use or disclosure of protected information with the consent of the director concerned"
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE -- "A company must not use or disclose protected information about any of its directors"

DECLARE `s 241 action` IS ONE OF
    `s 241(1) use or disclose protected information about a director`

-- The prohibition as a rule (a prohibition holds for the life of the company: no WITHIN, source-patterns 5.3).
-- src:3188 | (1) A company must not use or disclose protected information about any of its directors, except—
-- src:3189 | (a) for communicating with the director concerned,
-- src:3190 | (b) in order to comply with any requirement of the Companies Acts as to particulars to be sent to the registrar, or
-- src:3191 | (c) in accordance with section 244 (disclosure under court order).
@ref s 241(1) the company's duty not to use or disclose (src:3188-3191)
GIVEN `the bar applies` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `s 241 action`
`s 241(1) the company's duty not to use or disclose protected information` MEANS
    IF `the bar applies` EQUALS JUST TRUE
    THEN PARTY Company
         SHANT `s 241(1) use or disclose protected information about a director`
         HENCE FULFILLED
         LEST BREACH BY Company BECAUSE "s 241(1): the company used or disclosed protected information about a director otherwise than for communicating with him, complying with a requirement as to particulars for the registrar, or under a court order"
    ELSE FULFILLED

-- src:3193 | (3) If a company uses or discloses information in contravention of subsection (1), an offence is committed by—
-- src:3194 | (a) the company, and
-- src:3195 | (b) every officer of the company who is in default.
@ref s 241(3) the company's offence (src:3193-3195)
GIVEN `s 241(1) the company may not use or disclose the protected information` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 241(3)(a) the company commits an offence` MEANS
    CONSIDER `s 241(1) the company may not use or disclose the protected information`
    WHEN JUST TRUE THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN JUST FALSE THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "If a company uses or discloses information in contravention of subsection (1), an offence is committed by— (a) the company"
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent): whether subsection (1) was contravened is not known

-- src:3193 | (3) If a company uses or discloses information in contravention of subsection (1), an offence is committed by—
-- src:3194 | (a) the company, and
-- src:3195 | (b) every officer of the company who is in default.
@ref s 241(3) the officer's offence (src:3193-3195)
GIVEN `s 241(1) the company may not use or disclose the protected information` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `s 1121 the officer is in default` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 241(3)(b) the officer commits an offence` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `s 241(1) the company may not use or disclose the protected information` EQUALS JUST FALSE
        THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "If a company uses or discloses information in contravention of subsection (1), an offence is committed by ... (b) every officer of the company who is in default"
        IF `s 241(1) the company may not use or disclose the protected information` EQUALS NOTHING
        THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent): whether subsection (1) was contravened is not known
        IF `s 1121 the officer is in default` EQUALS JUST TRUE
        THEN JUST TRUE
        IF `s 1121 the officer is in default` EQUALS NOTHING
        THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): whether the officer is in default is s 1121's answer
        OTHERWISE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "every officer of the company who is in default"

-- (4): on summary conviction (a) in England and Wales, a fine (no limit stated); (b) in Scotland or Northern Ireland, a fine not exceeding level 5 and a daily default fine not exceeding
-- one-tenth of level 5.
-- src:3196 | (4) A person guilty of an offence under this section is liable on summary conviction—
-- src:3197 | (a) in England and Wales, to a fine;
-- src:3198 | (b) in Scotland or Northern Ireland, to a fine not exceeding level 5 on the standard scale and, for continued contravention, a daily default fine not exceeding one-tenth of level 5 on the standard scale.
@ref s 241(4) the penalty (src:3196-3198)
GIVEN place IS A `Mode of conviction`
GIVETH A MAYBE Penalty
`s 241(4) the penalty` MEANS
    CONSIDER place
    WHEN `on summary conviction in England and Wales` THEN JUST (Penalty WITH
        `how convicted` IS `on summary conviction in England and Wales`
        `imprisonment not exceeding` IS NOTHING
        `fine not exceeding` IS JUST `a fine without a stated limit`
        `daily default fine for continued contravention` IS NOTHING
        `imprisonment and fine together` IS FALSE)
    WHEN `on summary conviction in Scotland` THEN JUST (Penalty WITH
        `how convicted` IS `on summary conviction in Scotland`
        `imprisonment not exceeding` IS NOTHING
        `fine not exceeding` IS JUST (`a fine not exceeding a level on the standard scale` 5 1)
        `daily default fine for continued contravention` IS JUST (`a fine not exceeding a level on the standard scale` 5 0.1)
        `imprisonment and fine together` IS FALSE)
    WHEN `on summary conviction in Northern Ireland` THEN JUST (Penalty WITH
        `how convicted` IS `on summary conviction in Northern Ireland`
        `imprisonment not exceeding` IS NOTHING
        `fine not exceeding` IS JUST (`a fine not exceeding a level on the standard scale` 5 1)
        `daily default fine for continued contravention` IS JUST (`a fine not exceeding a level on the standard scale` 5 0.1)
        `imprisonment and fine together` IS FALSE)
    OTHERWISE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "liable on summary conviction— (a) in England and Wales ... (b) in Scotland or Northern Ireland"

-- ======================================================================================================================
-- s 242 Protected information: restriction on ... disclosure by registrar
-- ======================================================================================================================

-- src:3200 | (1) The registrar must omit protected information from the material on the register that is available for inspection where—
-- src:3201 | (a) it is contained in a document delivered to him in which such information is required to be stated, and
-- src:3202 | (b) in the case of a document having more than one part, it is contained in a part of the document in which such information is required to be stated.
@ref s 242(1) the registrar must omit protected information from the register material (src:3200-3202)
GIVEN `it is contained in a document delivered to the registrar in which such information is required to be stated` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the document has more than one part` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is contained in a part of the document in which such information is required to be stated` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 242(1) the registrar must omit the protected information from the material available for inspection` MEANS
    IF `it is contained in a document delivered to the registrar in which such information is required to be stated`
       AND ((NOT `the document has more than one part`) OR `it is contained in a part of the document in which such information is required to be stated`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The registrar must omit protected information from the material on the register that is available for inspection where— (a) it is contained in a document delivered to him in which such information is required to be stated, and (b) in the case of a document having more than one part, it is contained in a part of the document in which such information is required to be stated"

DECLARE `s 242(2) what the registrar is asked to do` IS ONE OF
    `s 242(2)(a) to check other documents or other parts of the document to ensure the absence of protected information`
    `s 242(2)(b) to omit from the material available for public inspection anything registered before this Chapter comes into force`
    `s 242(2) something else`

-- src:3203 | (2) The registrar is not obliged—
-- src:3204 | (a) to check other documents or (as the case may be) other parts of the document to ensure the absence of protected information, or
-- src:3205 | (b) to omit from the material that is available for public inspection anything registered before this Chapter comes into force.
@ref s 242(2) what the registrar is not obliged to do (src:3203-3205)
GIVEN task IS A `s 242(2) what the registrar is asked to do`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 242(2) the registrar is obliged to do it` MEANS
    CONSIDER task
    WHEN `s 242(2)(a) to check other documents or other parts of the document to ensure the absence of protected information` THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The registrar is not obliged— (a) to check other documents or (as the case may be) other parts of the document to ensure the absence of protected information"
    WHEN `s 242(2)(b) to omit from the material available for public inspection anything registered before this Chapter comes into force` THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The registrar is not obliged— ... (b) to omit from the material that is available for public inspection anything registered before this Chapter comes into force"
    WHEN `s 242(2) something else` THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "The registrar is not obliged— (a) ... (b) ..."

DECLARE `s 242(3) the registrar's disclosure` IS ONE OF
    `s 242(3)(a) as permitted by section 243 (permitted disclosure by the registrar)`
    `s 242(3)(b) in accordance with section 244 (disclosure under court order)`
    `s 242(3)(c) as permitted by section 1110F (general powers of disclosure by the registrar)`
    `s 242(3) in some other way`

-- src:3206 | (3) The registrar must not ... disclose protected information except—
-- src:3207 | (a) as permitted by section 243 (permitted ... disclosure by registrar), ...
-- src:3208 | (b) in accordance with section 244 (disclosure under court order) , or
-- src:3209 | (c) as permitted by section 1110F (general powers of disclosure by the registrar).
@ref s 242(3) the registrar must not disclose protected information (src:3206-3209)
GIVEN disclosure IS A `s 242(3) the registrar's disclosure`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 242(3) the registrar must not make the disclosure` MEANS
    CONSIDER disclosure
    WHEN `s 242(3) in some other way` THEN JUST TRUE -- "The registrar must not ... disclose protected information except—"
    OTHERWISE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "except— (a) as permitted by section 243 ..., (b) in accordance with section 244 ..., or (c) as permitted by section 1110F"

-- ======================================================================================================================
-- s 243 Permitted ... disclosure by the registrar
-- ======================================================================================================================

-- src:3225 | “credit reference agency” means a person carrying on a business comprising the furnishing of information relevant to the financial standing of individuals, being information collected by the agency for that purpose; ...
@ref s 243(7) credit reference agency (src:3225-3225)
GIVEN `the person carries on a business comprising the furnishing of information relevant to the financial standing of individuals` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the information is collected by the agency for that purpose` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 243(7) the person is a credit reference agency` MEANS
    IF `the person carries on a business comprising the furnishing of information relevant to the financial standing of individuals` AND `the information is collected by the agency for that purpose`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "“credit reference agency” means a person carrying on a business comprising the furnishing of information relevant to the financial standing of individuals, being information collected by the agency for that purpose"

-- src:3212 | (2) The registrar may disclose protected information to a credit reference agency.
@ref s 243(2) disclosure to a credit reference agency (src:3212-3212)
GIVEN `s 243(7) the person is a credit reference agency` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 243(2) the registrar may disclose protected information to the person` MEANS
    CONSIDER `s 243(7) the person is a credit reference agency`
    WHEN JUST TRUE THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN JUST FALSE THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "The registrar may disclose protected information to a credit reference agency"
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent): whether the person is a credit reference agency is not known

-- (4): the Secretary of State may by regulations require the registrar, on application, to refrain from disclosing to a credit reference agency. The regulations are not in the sources:
-- whether they exist and apply is an input (NOTHING when not known).
-- src:3216 | (4) The Secretary of State may make provision by regulations requiring the registrar, on application, to refrain from disclosing protected information relating to a director to a credit reference agency.
@ref s 243(4) regulations on refraining from disclosure (src:3216-3216)
GIVEN `regulations under subsection (4) require the registrar, on application, to refrain from disclosing protected information relating to the director to a credit reference agency` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `an application has been made as the regulations require` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 243(4) the registrar must refrain from disclosing the protected information to a credit reference agency` MEANS
    CONSIDER `regulations under subsection (4) require the registrar, on application, to refrain from disclosing protected information relating to the director to a credit reference agency`
    WHEN JUST TRUE THEN
         IF `an application has been made as the regulations require`
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): who may apply, on what grounds and how the application is determined are for the regulations (s 243(5))
    WHEN JUST FALSE THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "The Secretary of State may make provision by regulations" (no regulations)
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): whether regulations under subsection (4) exist is not in the sources

-- ======================================================================================================================
-- s 244 Disclosure under court order
-- ======================================================================================================================

-- src:3229 | (1) The court may make an order for the disclosure of protected information by the company or by the registrar if—
-- src:3230 | (a) there is evidence that service of documents at a service address other than the director's usual residential address is not effective to bring them to the notice of the director, or
-- src:3231 | (b) it is necessary or expedient for the information to be provided in connection with the enforcement of an order or decree of the court,
-- src:3232 | and the court is otherwise satisfied that it is appropriate to make the order.
-- RECONCILED 2026-11-12 (name-test sweep, fork F-NT-244-1): the function is named for a power or grant given "if" a gate is met (no "only if"); when the gate fails the answer is NOTHING, not JUST FALSE. The other reading, a failed "if" read as the text's own no, is JUST FALSE.
@ref s 244(1) the court may order disclosure (src:3229-3232)
GIVEN `there is evidence that service of documents at a service address other than the director's usual residential address is not effective to bring them to the notice of the director` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is necessary or expedient for the information to be provided in connection with the enforcement of an order or decree of the court` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the court is otherwise satisfied that it is appropriate to make the order` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 244(1) the court may make an order for the disclosure of protected information` MEANS
    IF (`there is evidence that service of documents at a service address other than the director's usual residential address is not effective to bring them to the notice of the director`
        OR `it is necessary or expedient for the information to be provided in connection with the enforcement of an order or decree of the court`)
       AND `the court is otherwise satisfied that it is appropriate to make the order`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "The court may make an order for the disclosure of protected information by the company or by the registrar if— (a) there is evidence that service ... is not effective ..., or (b) it is necessary or expedient ..., and the court is otherwise satisfied that it is appropriate to make the order"

-- src:3233 | (2) An order for disclosure by the registrar is to be made only if the company—
-- src:3234 | (a) does not have the director's usual residential address, or
-- src:3235 | (b) has been dissolved.
@ref s 244(2) an order against the registrar (src:3233-3235)
GIVEN `the company does not have the director's usual residential address` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the company has been dissolved` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 244(2) an order for disclosure by the registrar may be made` MEANS
    IF `the company does not have the director's usual residential address` OR `the company has been dissolved`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "An order for disclosure by the registrar is to be made only if the company— (a) does not have the director's usual residential address, or (b) has been dissolved"

DECLARE `s 244(3) applicant` IS ONE OF
    `s 244(3) a liquidator of the company`
    `s 244(3) a creditor of the company`
    `s 244(3) a member of the company`
    `s 244(3) any other person`

-- "any other person appearing to the court to have a sufficient interest": the court's view is an input.
-- src:3236 | (3) The order may be made on the application of a liquidator, creditor or member of the company, or any other person appearing to the court to have a sufficient interest.
@ref s 244(3) who may apply (src:3236-3236)
GIVEN applicant IS A `s 244(3) applicant`
      `the person appears to the court to have a sufficient interest` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 244(3) the order may be made on the application of the person` MEANS
    CONSIDER applicant
    WHEN `s 244(3) any other person` THEN
         IF `the person appears to the court to have a sufficient interest`
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (list not closed): "on the application of a liquidator, creditor or member of the company, or any other person appearing to the court to have a sufficient interest" (no "only")
    OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- src:3237 | (4) The order must specify the persons to whom, and purposes for which, disclosure is authorised.
@ref s 244(4) what the order must say (src:3237-3237)
GIVEN `the order specifies the persons to whom disclosure is authorised` IS A BOOLEAN
