`s 244(4) the order meets the requirement` MEANS
    IF `the order specifies the persons to whom disclosure is authorised` AND `the order specifies the purposes for which disclosure is authorised`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The order must specify the persons to whom, and purposes for which, disclosure is authorised" (a bare "must" not done: fork F-MUST-1)

-- ======================================================================================================================
-- s 245 Circumstances in which registrar may put address on the public record
-- ======================================================================================================================

-- src:3239 | (1) The registrar may put a director's usual residential address on the public record if—
-- src:3240 | (a) communications sent by the registrar to the director and requiring a response within a specified period remain unanswered, or
-- src:3241 | (b) there is evidence that service of documents at a service address provided in place of the director's usual residential address is not effective to bring them to the notice of the director.
-- RECONCILED 2026-11-12 (name-test sweep, fork F-NT-245-1): the function is named for a power or grant given "if" a gate is met (no "only if"); when the gate fails the answer is NOTHING, not JUST FALSE. The other reading, a failed "if" read as the text's own no, is JUST FALSE.
@ref s 245(1) when the registrar may put the address on the public record (src:3239-3241)
GIVEN `communications sent by the registrar to the director and requiring a response within a specified period remain unanswered` IS A BOOLEAN
      `there is evidence that service of documents at a service address provided in place of the director's usual residential address is not effective to bring them to the notice of the director` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 245(1) the registrar may put the director's usual residential address on the public record` MEANS
    IF `communications sent by the registrar to the director and requiring a response within a specified period remain unanswered`
       OR `there is evidence that service of documents at a service address provided in place of the director's usual residential address is not effective to bring them to the notice of the director`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "The registrar may put a director's usual residential address on the public record if— (a) communications sent by the registrar to the director and requiring a response within a specified period remain unanswered, or (b) there is evidence that service of documents at a service address provided in place of the director's usual residential address is not effective"

DECLARE `s 245(2) recipient of the notice` IS ONE OF
    `s 245(2)(a) the director`
    `s 245(2)(b) every company of which the registrar has been notified that the individual is a director`
    `s 245(2) someone else`

