-- src:3244 | (b) to every company of which the registrar has been notified that the individual is a director.
@ref s 245(2) notice of the proposal (src:3242-3244)
GIVEN recipient IS A `s 245(2) recipient of the notice`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 245(2) the registrar must give notice of the proposal to the recipient` MEANS
    CONSIDER recipient
    WHEN `s 245(2)(a) the director` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 245(2)(b) every company of which the registrar has been notified that the individual is a director` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 245(2) someone else` THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (list not closed): "The registrar must give notice of the proposal— (a) to the director, and (b) to every company of which the registrar has been notified that the individual is a director" (no "only")

-- src:3245 | (3) The notice must—
-- src:3246 | (a) state the grounds on which it is proposed to put the director's usual residential address on the public record, and
-- src:3247 | (b) specify a period within which representations may be made before that is done.
@ref s 245(3) what the notice must contain (src:3245-3247)
GIVEN `the notice states the grounds on which it is proposed to put the director's usual residential address on the public record` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the notice specifies a period within which representations may be made before that is done` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 245(3) the notice meets the requirement` MEANS
    IF `the notice states the grounds on which it is proposed to put the director's usual residential address on the public record` AND `the notice specifies a period within which representations may be made before that is done`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The notice must— (a) state the grounds on which it is proposed to put the director's usual residential address on the public record, and (b) specify a period within which representations may be made before that is done" (a bare "must" not done: fork F-MUST-1)

