-- (4) and (5): for the five years beginning with the date of the decision no service address other than the usual residential address may be registered, unless a new service address is registered
-- under regulations under s 1097B. "The period of five years beginning with the date" runs to the day before the fifth anniversary of the decision (fork F-246-1).
-- src:3259 | (4) Where a director’s usual residential address has been put on the public record by the registrar under this section, for the period of five years beginning with the date of the registrar’s decision no service address may be registered for the director other than their usual residential address (but see subsection (5)).
-- src:3260 | (5) Subsection (4)—
-- src:3261 | (a) does not limit the service address that may be registered for the director under regulations under section 1097B (rectification of register), and
-- src:3262 | (b) ceases to apply in relation to the director if a new service address is registered for the director under those regulations.
@ref s 246(4) and (5) the five years (src:3259-3262)
GIVEN `the date of the registrar's decision` IS A DATE
      `the date in question` IS A DATE
      `a new service address is registered for the director under regulations under section 1097B` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 246(4) no service address may be registered for the director other than the usual residential address` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `a new service address is registered for the director under regulations under section 1097B`
        THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "(5) Subsection (4)— ... (b) ceases to apply in relation to the director if a new service address is registered for the director under those regulations"
        IF `the date in question` LESS THAN `add years` `the date of the registrar's decision` 5 AND `the date in question` AT LEAST `the date of the registrar's decision`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "for the period of five years beginning with the date of the registrar’s decision no service address may be registered for the director other than their usual residential address" (outside the period the text fixes)

-- src:3261 | (a) does not limit the service address that may be registered for the director under regulations under section 1097B (rectification of register), and
@ref s 246(5)(a) subsection (4) does not limit the s 1097B address (src:3261-3261)
GIVEN `the service address is registered under regulations under section 1097B` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 246(5)(a) subsection (4) limits the service address that may be registered` MEANS
    IF `the service address is registered under regulations under section 1097B`
    THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Subsection (4) (a) does not limit the service address that may be registered for the director under regulations under section 1097B (rectification of register)"
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "the service address that may be registered for the director under regulations under section 1097B"
